# Trivy ignore list for the sidecar image (PENG-5554). Used by deploy.yaml,
# image-scan.yml and the wrapper repo's weekly scan of the deployed image.
# Add an entry only when no fixed version exists, with a reason and a review
# date; remove it once a fix lands. Re-check the whole list on every
# golden-image or upstream bump.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Day-one entries (2026-11-23). Every one comes from the Bark golden base image
# (ghcr.io/bark-com/python:<ver>-alpine-3.22.4-nonroot), not in this repo's
# code or its uv.lock. Except the CPython rows below, they are fixed by a golden-image rebuild, which arrives
# here as a golden-image-update PR; golden-images v1 builds were last green on
# 2026-11-04. REVIEW BY 2026-12-07: on every golden-image bump, rerun Trivy
# with this file emptied and delete each entry that no longer reports.

# --- CPython: rows from the golden image's `python3` placeholder package ----
# The golden image registers a virtual apk package `python3` versioned "3.12"
# so apk does not pull Alpine's system Python. The interpreter this image runs
# is the golden build in /usr/local: 3.12.12 (golden PYTHON_3_12_VERSION; latest 3.12.16).
# Trivy has no target for that interpreter. These rows, matched against the
# placeholder, are its only CPython signal, and they never clear by ID (the
# placeholder stays "3.12"), so interpreter currency has to be tracked by the
# golden-images Python version, not by this scan.
#
# False positives: Alpine fixed these at or below 3.12.12.
CVE-2015-20107
CVE-2019-16056
CVE-2019-20907
